  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Which of the following statements is true regarding the series${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }3(0.6)^{n+1}$ ?",
  "worked_solution": "The series starts with $n=1.$ So the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{3{(0.6)}^{2+1}}{3{(0.6)}^{1+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{(0.6)}^{3}}{3{(0.6)}^{2}} \\\\  & =0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is convergent because $|r|<1.$",
